{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 47,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come down, and sit in the dust, O virgin daughter of Babylon, sit on the ground: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no throne, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called tender and delicate.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take the millstones, and grind meal: uncover thy locks, make bare the leg, uncover the thigh, pass over the rivers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy nakedness shall be uncovered, yes, thy shame shall be seen: I will take vengeance, and I will not meet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our Redeemer, the LORD of hosts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his name, the Holy One of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sit thou silent, and get thee into darkness, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called, The lady of kingdoms.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was wroth with my people, I have polluted my inheritance, and given them into thy hand: thou didst show them no mercy; upon the ancient hast thou very heavily laid thy yoke.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou saidst, I shall be a lady for ever: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that thou didst not lay these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to thy heart, neither didst remember the latter end of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore hear now this, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou that art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " given to pleasures, that dwellest carelessly, that sayest in thy heart, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and none else besides me; I shall not sit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a widow, neither shall I know the loss of children:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But these two ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall come to thee in a moment in one day, the loss of children, and widowhood: they shall come upon thee in their perfection, for the multitude of thy sorceries, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the great abundance of thy enchantments.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou hast trusted in thy wickedness: thou hast said, None seeth me. Thy wisdom and thy knowledge, it hath perverted thee; and thou hast said in thy heart, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and none else besides me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore shall evil come upon thee; thou shalt not know from whence it riseth: and mischief shall fall upon thee; thou shalt not be able to put it off: and desolation shall come upon thee suddenly, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou shalt not know.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Stand now with thy enchantments, and with the multitude of thy sorceries, in which thou hast labored from thy youth; if thou shalt be able to profit, if thou mayest prevail.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art wearied in the multitude of thy counsels. Let now the astrologers, the star-gazers, the monthly prognosticators, stand up, and save thee from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that shall come upon thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, they shall be as stubble; the fire shall burn them; they shall not deliver themselves from the power of the flame: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a coal to warm at, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "nor",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fire to sit before it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.47.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.47.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus shall they be to thee with whom thou hast labored, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy merchants, from thy youth: they shall wander every one to his quarter; none shall save thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
